                "retweet_count": 4,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Our policy objective must be a drug-pricing system where coupons (copay assistance) from drugmakers aren\u2019t even necessary, because health insurance companies can be counted on to reduce and even eliminate out-of-pocket (OOP) costs entirely for properly prescribed treatment. People pay premiums with the expectation that when a doctor prescribes them a medicine, their insurance company will make it affordable. There\u2019s no need for patients to have financial skin-in-the-game for prescribed medications \u2013\u00a0it reduces adherence and punishes the poor.",
