                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Working on a bill in Congress for that. Patients should not go without medicine because of steep out-of-pocket costs imposed by health insurance companies. You pay premiums so that when a doctor writes you a prescription, you can access that treatment without undue burden. Otherwise, what's the point?\n\nIn the meantime \u2013 the biggest inhaler manufacturers have announced coupons to cap OOP costs at $35. The insurance companies have to honor those coupons.",
